type: software
title: "Negative mutual information in time in the smallest dimensions"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. Fullwood and Parzygnat proposed a mutual information between the input and output of a quantum process, built from the anticommutator state over time (pseudo-density matrix) and the signed entropy S(X) = -Tr X log|X|, and conjectured that it is never negative. Fullwood and Yang proved this for qubit inputs (preprint), and a public five-dimensional Werner-Holevo example showed that it fails in general. This work shows that a violation needs input dimension at least 3, output dimension at least 2 and initial rank at least 2, and gives one qutrit-to-qubit process on a rank-two state that attains all three bounds, certified by exact root isolation and interval arithmetic. For rank-two states a violation requires coherence between the occupied levels and an empty one. A family of coherent completions of a qubit erasure channel has explicit spectra; at t = 5/21 its sign reduces to 2573571875 < 8707129344, and it is negative exactly for 0 < t < (sqrt(33)-1)/16. Whether the quantity is unbounded below, and its most negative qutrit value, remain open."
